          %h2#definition Definition
          %p There are many notions of a character for an algebraic structure, often topologized.
          %h3#CharacterOfAGroup Character of a group
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            %em characters
            of a group:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#MultiplicativeCharacterOfAGroup"} multiplicative group characters
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#CharacterOfALinearRepresentation"} characters of linear representations of a group
                \.
          %p
            Here the first notion is the special case of the second notion for
            %em
              1-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+vector+space"} dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+representations"} linear representations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            %em all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            are 1-dimensional, in this case both notions agree, but in general they do not.
          %h4#MultiplicativeCharacterOfAGroup Multiplicative character of a group
          %p
            A
            %em multiplicative character
            on a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"}> discrete
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (a
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+character"} group character
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^\times
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi
                  \\;\colon\;
                  G
                  \\longrightarrow
                  k^\times
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^\times
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            we have that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                such a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
                under
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation"} conjugation
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
                of elements in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %li
              %p
                the collection of characters is itself an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
                under pointwise multiplication, this is called the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/character+lattice"} character lattice
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(G,k^\times)
                of the group. Similarly the
                %strong cocharacter lattice
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi k
                          %mo ×
                        %mo ,
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(k^\times, G)
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+character"} group character
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
            one considers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            characters. Specifically, for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff"} locally compact Hausdorff
            group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (often further assumed to be an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %strong character
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a continuous homomorphism to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+group"} profinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete
            group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/86089/two-definitions-of-character-of-topological-groups"} MO
          %h4#CharacterOfALinearRepresentation Character of a linear representation of a group
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/character+of+a+linear+representation"} character of a linear representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho\colon G\to End(V)
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+character"} group character
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            given by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi Tr
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \mapsto Tr \rho(g)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            makes sense (e.g. when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
            under
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation+action"} conjugation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
            of elements in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Sometimes we also extend a character linearly to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} free vector space
            on the set of conjugacy classes. This version of the character can be identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategorical+trace"} bicategorical trace
            of the identity map of the representation, considered as a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[G]
            = succeed "-module." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            There is a different notion of an
            %em infinitesimal character
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harish%E2%80%93Chandra+theory"} Harish–Chandra theory
            and also a notion of the
            = succeed "." do
              %em formal character
          %p
            There are important formulas concerning characters in representation theory, like
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+character+formula"} Weyl character formula
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induced+character"} induced character
            of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induced+representation"} induced representation
          %h3#left_and_right_characters_on_a_ring_over_a_ring Left and right characters on a ring over a ring
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a unital, not necessarily commutative,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            (or, more generally,
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-commutative);" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-bimodules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-modules)," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-ring." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is an object in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coslice+category"} coslice category
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Ring
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\Ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            equipped with multiplication
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_B
            and a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta: A\to B
            of rings.
          %p
            A
            %strong left character
            of an
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B,\mu_B,\eta_B)
            is a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi:B\to A
            such that
          %p
            (i) (left
            = succeed "-linearity)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(\eta(a)b) = a\chi(b)
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
          %p
            (ii) (associativity)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi η
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(b b') = \chi(b (\eta\circ\chi)(b'))
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b,b'\in B
          %p
            (iii) (unitality)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(1_B) = \chi(1_A)
          %p
            where we denoted multiplication in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            by concatenation. The conditions on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            can be restated as the requirement that the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\otimes A\to A
            given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi a
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\otimes a\mapsto \chi(b\eta(a))
            is a
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            considered as a left action).
          %p
            Dually, a
            %strong right character
            of an
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B,\mu_B,\eta_B)
            is a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi:B\to A
            such that
          %p
            (i) (right
            = succeed "-linearity)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(b\eta(a)) = \chi(b)a
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
          %p
            (ii) (associativity)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi η
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(b b') = \chi((\eta\circ\chi)(b) b')
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b,b'\in B
          %p
            (iii) (unitality)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(1_B) = \chi(1_A)
          %p
            This is in turn equivalent to extending the right regular action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to the action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h3#character_of_a_topological_space Character of a topological space
          %p
            The character
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(X,x)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            at a point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is the minimal cardinality of a local basis of neighborhoods of point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            (local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+basis"} basis of topology
            on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(X,x)
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            runs through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
