          %h2#references References
          %p
            Character rings of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
            are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The representation ring of a compact Lie group
                = succeed ":1" do
                  %strong 34
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/numdam-bin/fitem?id=PMIHES_1968__34__113_0"} NUMDAM
            %li
              %p
                Masaru Takeuchi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A remark on the character ring of a compact Lie group
                = succeed ":4" do
                  %strong 23
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jmsj/1259849785"} Euclid
            %li
              %p
                Troels Roussauc Johansen,
                %em Character Theory for Finite Groups and Compact Lie Groups
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.upb.de/~johansen/character-theory.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in the more general context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transchromatic+character"}> transchromatic character
            ) is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Kuhn"} Nicholas Kuhn
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Ravenel"} Douglas Ravenel
              = succeed "," do
                %em Generalized group characters and complex oriented cohomology theories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/jams/2000-13-03/S0894-0347-00-00332-5/"} publisher
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/mypapers/hkr.pdf"} pdf
          %p for review see
          %ul
            %li#Raksit15
              Arpon Raksit,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Characters in global equivariant homotopy theory
              %a{:href => "http://web.stanford.edu/~arpon/math/files/senior-thesis.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characters+of+linear+representations"} characters of linear representations
            of
